[300,1025,1026],{"class":314}," identifier ",[300,1028,637],{"class":310},[300,1030,951],{"class":310},[300,1032,924],{"class":353},[300,1034,357],{"class":314},[300,1036,360],{"class":310},[300,1038,383],{"class":333},[300,1040,360],{"class":310},[300,1042,318],{"class":310},[300,1044,330],{"class":310},[300,1046,1047],{"class":333},"GreetingService",[300,1049,360],{"class":310},[300,1051,318],{"class":310},[300,1053,330],{"class":310},[300,1055,1056],{"class":333},"app.acme-org.orders-app",[300,1058,360],{"class":310},[300,1060,368],{"class":314},[300,1062,1063,1066,1068,1070,1072,1075,1078,1080,1082,1084,1087],{"class":302,"line":430},[300,1064,1065],{"class":314},"host",[300,1067,631],{"class":310},[300,1069,900],{"class":314},[300,1071,631],{"class":310},[300,1073,1074],{"class":353},"register",[300,1076,1077],{"class":314},"(identifier",[300,1079,318],{"class":310},[300,1081,951],{"class":310},[300,1083,398],{"class":353},[300,1085,1086],{"class":314},"())   ",[300,1088,1089],{"class":622},"\u002F\u002F → srv:\u002F\u002Fapp.acme-org.orders-app~com.example.GreetingService\n",[300,1091,1092],{"class":302,"line":456},[300,1093,344],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":343},[300,1095,1096],{"class":302,"line":462},[300,1097,1098],{"class":622},"\u002F\u002F later, when the service should no longer be reachable\n",[300,1100,1101,1103,1105,1107,1109,1112],{"class":302,"line":467},[300,1102,1065],{"class":314},[300,1104,631],{"class":310},[300,1106,900],{"class":314},[300,1108,631],{"class":310},[300,1110,1111],{"class":353},"unRegister",[300,1113,1114],{"class":314},"(identifier)\n",[274,1116,1117,1118,1120,1121,1124,1125,1127,1128,1130],{},"The zone is the complete zone the service lives in: ",[278,1119,551],{}," and ",[278,1122,1123],{},"defaultZone"," apply to ",[278,1126,280],{}," classes only. Registering the same identifier twice on one client is a no-op, and ",[278,1129,1111],{}," ends any stream the service is still producing with an error to its caller.",[286,1132,1134],{"id":1133},"the-service-directory","The service directory",[274,1136,1137,1138,1141,1142,1120,1145,1148,1149,1152,1153,1156,1157,1159,1160,1163,1164,1167,1168,1171,1172,1174],{},"Every published class under the project's ",[278,1139,1140],{},"servicesPaths"," gets a service definition from ",[278,1143,1144],{},"kinotic generate",[278,1146,1147],{},"kinotic sync",", its functions with their parameters and types, written to the ",[278,1150,1151],{},"ServiceDefinitions"," module under ",[278,1154,1155],{},"generatedPath",". A project that imports that module has the runtime register each service in the platform's service directory as the service comes online: the services registered before ",[278,1158,968],{}," when the client connects, and a service registered on a connected client as it registers. Only a service in an application's zone, ",[278,1161,1162],{},"app.\u003CorganizationId>.\u003CapplicationId>"," or a zone under it, is registered, through the platform's ",[278,1165,1166],{},"ApplicationServiceDirectory"," in ",[278,1169,1170],{},"app-api",", which refuses a zone that is not the application's or an application outside the caller's organization. The directory then holds the application's services beside the platform's own, with their liveness; a service the project declares no definition for serves on its zone alone. A definition naming other functions than the class serves fails the registration, and with it the connection, until ",[278,1173,1147],{}," runs again.",[1176,1177,1179],"h3",{"id":1178},"parameter-and-return-types","Parameter and return types",[274,1181,1182],{},"Arguments and results travel as JSON, so a function's types are published as JSON carries them:",[1184,1185,1186,1202,1212,1233,1242,1255],"ul",{},[1187,1188,1189,1190,1193,1194,1197,1198,1201],"li",{},"A ",[278,1191,1192],{},"Promise"," or ",[278,1195,1196],{},"PromiseLike"," result is asynchronous and an ",[278,1199,1200],{},"Observable"," result is a stream, of the type it resolves to or emits.",[1187,1203,1204,1207,1208,1211],{},[278,1205,1206],{},"any",", ",[278,1209,1210],{},"unknown",", and a type parameter with no constraint accept anything; a constrained type parameter is its constraint.",[1187,1213,1214,1215,1218,1219,1120,1222,1225,1226,1207,1229,1232],{},"Interfaces, classes (their fields, without their methods), generic instantiations such as ",[278,1216,1217],{},"Page\u003CReport>",", mapped types such as ",[278,1220,1221],{},"Partial\u003CReport>",[278,1223,1224],{},"Pick\u003CReport, 'id'>",", intersections, and unions of objects are objects, named for the type and its type arguments (",[278,1227,1228],{},"Page_Report",[278,1230,1231],{},"Partial_Report",").",[1187,1234,1235,1120,1238,1241],{},[278,1236,1237],{},"Record\u003Cstring, V>",[278,1239,1240],{},"{[key: string]: V}"," are maps, enums are enums, and a union of string literals is a string.",[1187,1243,1189,1244,1247,1248,1250,1251,1254],{},[278,1245,1246],{},"Date"," is published as a date, but it arrives as the ISO-8601 string a date travels as: the service receives a string, and a TypeScript caller gets a string back. ",[278,1249,1144],{}," logs a warning for each one, and the directory carries the same warning in the ",[278,1252,1253],{},"warnings"," metadata of the parameter, or of the function for a result.",[1187,1256,1189,1257,1207,1260,1207,1263,1207,1266,1207,1269,1272],{},[278,1258,1259],{},"Map",[278,1261,1262],{},"Set",[278,1264,1265],{},"Uint8Array",[278,1267,1268],{},"Buffer",[278,1270,1271],{},"bigint",", tuple, or function fails generation with the reason and the type to declare instead.",[286,1274,1276],{"id":1275},"decorators","Decorators",[1176,1278,1280],{"id":1279},"publishnamespace-name-advertise","@Publish(namespace?, name?, advertise?)",[274,1282,1283,1284,1287,1288,1291,1292,1295,1296,1299,1300,1303],{},"Marks a class for publication. The full service identifier becomes ",[278,1285,1286],{},"namespace.ClassName","; both parts are optional (the name defaults to the class name). A service published with no namespace is addressed by its name in its zone, ",[278,1289,1290],{},"srv:\u002F\u002F\u003Czone>~ClassName",", and the platform's service directory names it in its zone's namespace, ",[278,1293,1294],{},"\u003Czone>.ClassName",", so services of the same name in different applications stay apart. Passing ",[278,1297,1298],{},"advertise"," as ",[278,1301,1302],{},"true"," additionally advertises the service in the platform service directory, so it appears in directory listings for browsing and invocation — publishing alone makes a service callable over RPC without listing it.",[1176,1305,1307],{"id":1306},"zonezone","@Zone(zone)",[274,1309,1310,1311,1313],{},"Declares the zone the service is addressable in, relative to the client's ",[278,1312,551],{},". The zone is one or more dot-separated labels of lowercase letters, digits, and interior dashes.",[1176,1315,1317],{"id":1316},"versionversion","@Version(version)",[274,1319,1320,1321,1324],{},"Sets the semantic version for the service in ",[278,1322,1323],{},"X.Y.Z"," format. Callers can pin to a specific version when resolving the service.",[1176,1326,1328],{"id":1327},"scope","@Scope",[274,1330,1331],{},"A getter or method decorator that marks the member providing the scope identifier. Scope targets requests at one specific instance of a service — for example the copy running on a particular node or device.",[291,1333,1335],{"className":293,"code":1334,"language":295,"meta":296,"style":296},"import { Publish, Scope } from '@kinotic-ai\u002Fcore'\n\n@Publish('com.example')\nclass DeviceService {\n    deviceId: string\n\n    @Scope\n    get scope(): string {\n        return this.deviceId\n    }\n\n    constructor(deviceId: string) {\n        this.deviceId = deviceId\n    }\n\n    getStatus(): string {\n        return `Status for device ${this.deviceId}`\n    }\n}\n",[278,1336,1337,1360,1364,1380,1389,1399,1403,1411,1426,1436,1440,1444,1463,1476,1481,1486,14